# Comando verificar a fondo (L2)

**Extends** `00-verification-gate.mdc` — does **not** replace or weaken L1. Loads on `/comando-verificar` or trigger phrases below.

## Triggers

| Language | Phrases |
|----------|---------|
| Slash | `/comando-verificar`, `comando-verificar` |
| ES | `verifica a fondo`, `prueba todas las combinaciones`, `matriz de verificación`, `casuísticas del formulario` |
| EN | `verify thoroughly`, `combinatorial verification`, `verification matrix`, `test all combinations` |

**Mandatory:** read `.cursor/skills/comando-verificar/SKILL.md` when triggered.

## Matrix requirement

Before overall PASS on a deep-verify session:

1. Produce `.cursor/context/verification/<scope-slug>/matrix.md` with timestamp header (timezone per `qa-reports-timestamp-mandatory.mdc`).
2. Every data row has stable **`row_id`** (`R-01`, `R-02`, …) — cite in FAIL summaries and `## Verification` (REQ-CV-MATRIX-08).
3. Verdict per row: `PASS` | `FAIL` | `BLOCKED` | `NOT VERIFIABLE` — no silent skips.
4. **>8** data rows → also `matrix.html` twin.

**Trivial scope** (CSS/copy only, no discrete factors): matrix may use `strategy: trivial` with ≥3 rows (render, lint, regression) — see skill.

## Scope: current diff (REQ-CV-SCOPE-01)

When scope is `current diff` or omitted:

- Document in matrix header: `git diff HEAD --name-only` (or staged/unstaged strategy — state which).
- List paths; bound inventory to those paths + direct dependents (routes/forms/services).

## Authentication (REQ-CV-AUTH-01)

- Multi-role rows: **one login attempt** per username per chat session.
- Prefer project E2E auth helper / storage-state reuse when documented; one attempt per user.
- Flood / still on login → `BLOCKED (credentials)` — **no retry** (`auth-credential-failure-no-retry.mdc`).

## URL resolution (REQ-CV-URL-01)

- Resolve base URL from the **target project's** stack rule (`00-openspec-stack-agnostic.mdc`) — never hardcode host/port from another repo.

## Destructive rows (REQ-CV-MATRIX-09)

Tag `destructive: true` for cancel, delete, irreversible workflow submits.

- Default: `BLOCKED (destructive)` unless scope explicitly authorizes **and** disposable local fixtures exist.
- Follow `unsafe-interactive-click-sweep` — no blind destructive click-sweep.

## Layer and evidence (VR-09, VR-11, VR-13, VR-15)

| Row type | Minimum evidence |
|----------|------------------|
| Form combo | **Verified (E2E/form)** — fill→submit (project E2E or Browser DevTools MCP) |
| AJAX / button | **Verified (interactive)** — click → DOM/message (VR-13) |
| JS / libraries | **Verified (JS)** — console 0 Uncaught on exact URL (VR-15) |
| Service | Project test command exit 0 or explicit FAIL output |
| Backend-only | Project lint / tests on touched paths |

Browser automation: prefer **Browser DevTools MCP** per `browser-devtools-use.mdc` when MCP is the chosen layer; project E2E runner when running specs.

## Combinatorial policy (REQ-CV-LIMIT-01)

| Combinations | Strategy |
|--------------|----------|
| ≤ 32 | Full cartesian — every row executed or BLOCKED with reason |
| 33–256 | Pairwise + single-factor edge rows |
| > 256 | Equivalence classes + pairwise on representatives |

Always include: happy path, validation errors, permission denied (if applicable). List **UNCOVERED** in header when using pairwise.

## Close format (REQ-CV-EXEC-03)

Final message **must** include `## Verification`:

- **Verified:** matrix path + PASS count / mandatory total.
- **Verified (E2E/form)** / **Verified (interactive)** when UI rows exist.
- **Verified (JS)** when JS rows exist.
- **Not verified:** BLOCKED / NOT VERIFIABLE rows with concrete blockers.

**Resumen** follows VR-14 — no success words without matching Verified lines.

